महस्, अस्, n. pleasure, enjoyment (Ved.); a
feast, festival; a sacrifice, oblation [cf. मह, म-
ख, मघ]; a festive hymn, hymn of praise;
greatness, might, power, strength, dominion (Ved.);
abundance, fulness, superfluity, multitude (Ved.);
light, ray of light, lustre, splendor; the fourth of the
seven worlds, the fourth Vyāhṛti (see महर् above);
= उदक, water (according to

माहाराजिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. महा-राज), attached
or devoted to or honouring the reigning prince;
imperial, fit for a great king, royal.

माहेय माहेय, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. मही), made
of earth, earthen, relating to the earth, terrestrial;
(अस्), m. the son of the earth, the planet Mars;
coral; (आस्), m. pl., N. of a people; (ई), f. a cow.
